{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Every man — his mother and his father — you shall fear.</b> To teach that the honor given them must not be of a kind that makes his heart arrogant toward them, even if he honors them with food and drink and clothing, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Kiddushin 31b): יֵשׁ מַאֲכִיל לְאָבִיו פַּסְיוֹנֵי וְטוֹרְדוֹ מִן הָעוֹלָם (\"there is one who feeds his father pasyon-dainties and thereby removes him from the world\"). Rather, his honoring of them should be like one who honors those who are awesome to him, in recognition of their superiority over him. Afterward he explains the matter of Sabbath, saying:" "<b>And My Sabbaths you shall keep.</b> He did not warn concerning the Sabbath of creation alone, but concerning every kind of Sabbath — the Sabbath of creation, the Sabbath of the land, and the remission of debts — all of which testify to the creation of the world. And after saying this:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:54.672223745Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}